A TSX file with broken JSX keeps the declarations tree-sitter recovers: the unclosed `<div>` in
`Header` stays inside its function, and `Footer` after it is listed. The stray `{` in `Card`'s JSX
puts the rest of the file in an `ERROR` node, so `Card` and `Page` are missing (techdebt.md,
"Declarations inside syntax errors are dropped").
== args
input/broken.tsx
== file input/broken.tsx
// Components.
export function Header() {
  return <div className="x">
}
export function Footer() {
  return <footer />;
}
export const Card = () => <section>{</section>;
export default class Page {}
